 "summary": "The post-PR surface is minimal and complete: both bundled structures are `@[ext]` on exactly the data their laws constrain, every definition has its `*_def` and characteristic lemmas via `(rfl)` so no consumer relies on defeq, `woodsSaxonCentralDensity` carries its universal property as an iff, nothing is `private` or `@[expose]`, and `Real.sigmoid_le_exp` is correctly exported in the upstream namespace in a PhyslibAlpha-shaped extension module. Simp/fun_prop annotations are on the right lemmas and the deliberate omission of simp on the three `*_density_apply` projections is justified by the conditional side goals on the normalisation integrals.",
